    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0227" n="129" xml:id="pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 King, Clifford J./2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-06T17:00:00-04:00">June 6, 1930—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>185. Hankow’s telegram June 6, noon, regarding capture of Reverend King.<anchor
                        n="33" xml:id="d110-f1"/></p>
                <p>Mission notified. Use every effort effect release and report results by
                    telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d110-f1" n="33" xml:id="d110-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 37, June 6, 1 p.m., from the Consul General at Hankow, <ref
                        target="#pg128">p. 128</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
